**How to implement.** A kit profile reads a lab file of any delimited shape through its column roles (001 §K 'map columns to scan variable(s) (unit; raw dial vs physical), signal, σ, timestamp, capture index, experiment key — or to Mueller elements m00…m33 plus configuration columns'; the S9.2 brief: 'a custom mapping'). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.2. In `OpticalConstructor.Storage/LabFileImport.fs` (step 301): (1) A private function reads a text into its rows by a delimiter and a header choice, through `CsvFile.Parse` (FSharp.Data, as `MuellerDataStore.fs:parseMuellerCsv` and `SpectralImport.fs` parse) with `separators` the delimiter's `character` as text and `hasHeaders` true for `HeaderOnFirstRow`: every exception is caught and answered `MalformedDataFileErr` with its message, rows whose cells are all blank are skipped as `parseMuellerCsv` skips them, and it answers the header's cells, when there is a header, and the data rows' cells. Step 307's preview calls the same function. (2) `type ImportProfile with member this.mapText (text : KitFileText) : Result<MappedRow list, ExperimentDataError>`: no data row is `EmptyDataFileErr`; each data row is one `MappedRow` (step 300), its cells taken by `DataColumnNumber.index` and trimmed: each scan column a `ScanCell` of its column and the number as a `UnitMagnitude`; `SignalColumns` a `SignalReading` of the signal as `MeasuredIntensity` and the σ as `MeasuredSigma`; `MuellerElementColumns` a `MuellerReading` whose element (i, j) is the column of index 4i + j, times the throughput when a throughput column is given (step 301's rule) and as read otherwise; the timestamp by `DateTimeOffset.TryParse` with `CultureInfo.InvariantCulture` and `DateTimeStyles.AssumeUniversal`, `parseMuellerCsv`'s rule; the capture index by `Int32.TryParse` with `NumberStyles.Integer` into `CaptureIndex`; the observable through `Observable.tryOfCell` (step 300); and the key as `DataRowKey` of the cell. Numbers are read by `Double.TryParse` with `NumberStyles.Float` and `CultureInfo.InvariantCulture`. The first cell that is missing, blank or does not read is `MalformedDataFileErr` naming the 1-based data row, the column and the cell; an unmapped column is read by nothing. No unit heuristics, culture guessing or quoting option is added. Tests, in `LabFileImportTests` (step 301), over test-local profiles written as records: `a column mapping reads each row's scan values, signal, σ and key`: a test-local signal profile `Lab scan` (comma, a header row, no byte-order mark; scan column 1 in degrees as a physical value; `SignalColumns (2, Some 3)`; key column 4; no timestamp, capture index or observable column) over `phi,I,sigma,exp\n0,0.5,0.01,CPL-(QZ#45)-CPL\n20,0.25,0.01,"LP-(AIR#0)-LP"\n` reads two rows: scan cells of column 1 with magnitudes 0 and 20, signals 0.5 and 0.25 with σ 0.01, and keys `CPL-(QZ#45)-CPL` and `LP-(AIR#0)-LP`, the CSV reader removing the quotes. `a semicolon file without a header maps its Mueller elements and throughput`: a profile (semicolon, no header row; scan column 1 in radians as a physical value; `MuellerElementColumns` of columns 2 to 17 with throughput 18; observable 19; key 20) over one row whose sixteen element cells are 1 and fifteen test-local fractions, throughput 0.5 and observable `R` reads one `MuellerReading` whose (0, 0) element is 0.5 and whose (1, 2) element is 0.5 times that cell, with `Some ReflectedMueller`. `a cell the mapping cannot read names its row and column`: a signal cell `n/a` in data row 2 answers `MalformedDataFileErr` holding `2`, the column number and `n/a`; a row with no key cell answers `MalformedDataFileErr`; and a header-only file answers `EmptyDataFileErr`. Verification (claim-check repair, .spec-md §9): ui-tests MUST select OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests (Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/FsxAcceptanceTests.fs:FsxAcceptanceTests) to preserve the constructor/export numerical parity with the Analytics examples. The constructor-unit-tests behavior checks above remain required; this selection neither edits that class nor substitutes for the future kit-acceptance tests.

**Acceptance.** After the column mapping lands, `ImportProfile.mapText` MUST read a lab file through its delimiter, header and column roles into mapped rows, refusing the first unreadable cell with its row and column; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a column mapping reads each row's scan values, signal, σ and key`, `a semicolon file without a header maps its Mueller elements and throughput` and `a cell the mapping cannot read names its row and column`, the count rising by 3; and build, elevation and the sixteen s30 invariants MUST pass. ui-tests MUST pass over OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests, preserving its constructor/export numerical parity with the Analytics examples and its test count.
